DELIBERATE PLAYABILITY DEVIATION (834): clamp championship season >= 0 on relegation

*** THIS IS AN INTENTIONAL DEVIATION FROM dd2h.exe, NOT A FAITHFUL RECONSTRUCTION. ***
It is the ONLY sanctioned deviation in the tree and is applied on explicit user request
("fixen") after the alternative (leave-faithful) was considered.

Root of the ORIGINAL behavior (confirmed against dd2h.exe, objdump):
  Do_End_Of_Season_Stuff @0x44c394, case 3 (Check_League_Standing returns 3 = relegated):
      44c3aa:  ff 0d c0 de 93 00   decl 0x93dec0        ; _current_season--   (NO CLAMP)
  The original decrements _current_season unconditionally. If the player is already in the
  bottom division (_current_season == 0) and gets relegated, it goes to -1. The next
  Play_Game then reads
      _current_level = *(int*)(&DAT_0046758c + _current_race*4 + _current_season*0x14)
  at season == -1 -> reads @0x467578 (before the level table) = deterministic IMAGE data
  (453836800) -> Play_Game(garbage level) -> WASM `unreachable` / native OOB. dd2h.exe has
  the SAME latent bug (the asm has no guard); it is normally unreachable because ordinary
  play never relegates out of division 0 -- it is only hit via the abnormal "retire all 5
  races of the bottom division" path a QA agent exercised.

Deviation applied: only decrement when _current_season > 0, so a bottom-division relegation
keeps season 0 (stays in the bottom division) instead of underflowing. This makes the
championship robust against every race-outcome path (including retire-all-races) at the cost
of exact bit-parity ONLY on that one abnormal, previously-crashing path -- which produced no
valid output to be parity-checked anyway. All normal-play paths are byte-unchanged (season is
never 0-and-relegated in normal completion), so verify / verify-wasm / L9 bit-identity are
unaffected.

Verified: full retire-all-5-races championship season now returns to the FE with no crash
(was WASM `unreachable`); verify + verify-wasm 10/10 both targets; L9 702/702 native<->wasm
bit-identical (this path is not on the attract).
--- a/dd2.c
+++ b/dd2.c
@@ -38141,7 +38141,9 @@
     }
     break;
   case 3:
-    _current_season = _current_season + -1;
+    if (0 < _current_season) {  /* 834 DELIBERATE DEVIATION: original `decl 0x93dec0` has no clamp; relegating out of division 0 underflows season to -1 -> OOB level read -> crash. Clamp keeps the player in the bottom division. */
+      _current_season = _current_season + -1;
+    }
     break;
   case 4:
     return 1;
